# yosys 0.55 (VTR build): read_rtlil multiport_pmux.il; opt_muxtree; write_rtlil   (hand-written input, read unedited)
# THIS IS YOSYS'S UNSOUND OUTPUT, kept as evidence only (multiport_pmux.expect is ours): C feeds two ports of M, replace_known writes 1 into C.A under the first port's knowledge
# eval: yosys -p "read_rtlil multiport_pmux.il; eval -set s0 0 -set s1 1 -set t 0 -set a 0 -set b 0 -show y" gives y = 1'0; the same on the opt_muxtree output gives y = 1'1
# normalised by name: see the top of test_opt_muxtree.c
cell $mux WIDTH=1 A=1 B=b:0 S=t:0 Y=c:0
cell $pmux WIDTH=1 S_WIDTH=2 A=a:0 B=c:0 c:0 S=s0:0 s1:0 Y=y:0
removed 0
